# Intake image ⇄ mediator-service — expected requests
#
# Requirements contract for what the netbooted Alpine intake image (and its
# station TUI) sends to the server, across Phase 1 (catalog) and Phase 2
# (automated tests). This is the reference the image is built against.
#
# Compatible with the VS Code "REST Client" / JetBrains .http runner.
# Fill the variables below, then run requests top-to-bottom.
#
# NEW vs today (deferred-identity components, see component-lifecycle.md):
#   • disks[] MUST carry a per-drive `serial` (+ optional wwn/model) — today it
#     only sends name/sizeGb/type. This is the load-bearing image change:
#     each reported sub-device becomes an in-device component instance, and its
#     Phase-2 reports are uploaded under SN:<driveSerial>/ (not the machine SN).
#   • Phase-2 uploads split into machine-level (SN:<machineSerial>) and
#     per-component (SN:<driveSerial>) targets.

@host = http://localhost:8080
@intakeToken = dev-intake-token

# --- Identity of the device on the bench (from the scan) --------------------
@machineSerial = PF1ABCDE
@mac = a4:83:e7:00:11:22
# One entry per physical drive the image detects. Its SERIAL is the report key.
@disk0Serial = S3Z9NX0M12345
@disk1Serial = 224481007777

@intakeKey = SN:{{machineSerial}}


###############################################################################
# PHASE 0 — image boot / TUI bootstrap
###############################################################################

# Category dropdown for the "create new reference" TUI step (bootable devices only).
GET {{host}}/api/intake/categories
X-Intake-Token: {{intakeToken}}


###############################################################################
# PHASE 1 — catalog (station TUI, operator-driven)
###############################################################################

# 1) State-machine router. Sent on every boot; server picks the next step from
#    DB state. The scan payload is the full hardware read.
#
#    SERVER SIDE-EFFECT (new): for each disks[] entry the server creates one
#    in-device component instance (Artikel_Nummer NULL, BoxID NULL, Auf_Lager=1,
#    Zerlegt_aus relation + slotKey to the machine item). Idempotent on re-scan,
#    keyed on the drive serial (fallback wwn / model+size when serial is blank).
POST {{host}}/api/intake/start
X-Intake-Token: {{intakeToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serial": "{{machineSerial}}",
  "mac": "{{mac}}",
  "vendor": "HP",
  "model": "EliteBook 840 G5",
  "cpu": "Intel i5-8350U",
  "ramMb": 8192,
  "disks": [
    { "name": "nvme0n1", "sizeGb": 256, "type": "nvme", "serial": "{{disk0Serial}}", "wwn": "eui.0025385...", "model": "SAMSUNG MZVLB256" },
    { "name": "sda",     "sizeGb": 500, "type": "hdd",  "serial": "{{disk1Serial}}", "wwn": "5000c500...",   "model": "ST500LM021" }
  ],
  "batteryPercent": 87
}

###
# 2a) Answer select_ref by picking an EXISTING reference.
POST {{host}}/api/intake/{{intakeKey}}/answer
X-Intake-Token: {{intakeToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "ref",
  "artikelNummer": "12345",
  "scanPayload": {
    "serial": "{{machineSerial}}", "mac": "{{mac}}", "vendor": "HP", "model": "EliteBook 840 G5",
    "cpu": "Intel i5-8350U", "ramMb": 8192,
    "disks": [
      { "name": "nvme0n1", "sizeGb": 256, "type": "nvme", "serial": "{{disk0Serial}}" },
      { "name": "sda",     "sizeGb": 500, "type": "hdd",  "serial": "{{disk1Serial}}" }
    ],
    "batteryPercent": 87
  }
}

###
# 2b) …or answer select_ref by CREATING a new reference.
#     Kurzbeschreibung is optional (defaults to scanPayload.model).
POST {{host}}/api/intake/{{intakeKey}}/answer
X-Intake-Token: {{intakeToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "ref",
  "newRef": {
    "Hersteller": "HP",
    "Kurzbeschreibung": "EliteBook 840 G5",
    "Hauptkategorien_A": 20,
    "Unterkategorien_A": 201
  },
  "scanPayload": {
    "serial": "{{machineSerial}}", "mac": "{{mac}}", "vendor": "HP", "model": "EliteBook 840 G5",
    "cpu": "Intel i5-8350U", "ramMb": 8192,
    "disks": [
      { "name": "nvme0n1", "sizeGb": 256, "type": "nvme", "serial": "{{disk0Serial}}" }
    ],
    "batteryPercent": 87
  }
}

###
# 3) Answer the quality step. instanceSpecs carries per-unit spec confirmations.
POST {{host}}/api/intake/{{intakeKey}}/answer
X-Intake-Token: {{intakeToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "quality",
  "qualityAnswers": {
    "is_functional": "true",
    "is_complete": "true",
    "has_defects": "false",
    "cosmetic": "B",
    "drive_type": "NVMe SSD"
  },
  "instanceSpecs": {
    "RAM": "8 GB DDR4",
    "SSD": "256 GB NVMe"
  }
}

###
# 4) Trigger agentic enrichment. Idempotent; may be re-called after Phase 2
#    uploads land so agentic re-runs with richer data.
POST {{host}}/api/intake/{{intakeKey}}/complete
X-Intake-Token: {{intakeToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}


###############################################################################
# PHASE 2 — automated tests (image-driven, no operator). Serial-keyed uploads.
#   Reuses the external-docs write endpoint. The SN: prefix skips the DB lookup
#   and resolves the storage path from the serial directly — the item (machine
#   or component) does not need to exist yet. Files land at {mountPath}/{serial}/.
###############################################################################

# --- Machine-level reports → aggregate on the MACHINE item ------------------

# memtest (whole-machine RAM)
POST {{host}}/api/items/SN:{{machineSerial}}/external-docs/intake-scans
X-Intake-Token: {{intakeToken}}
X-Filename: memtest.txt
Content-Type: text/plain

<<< raw memtest output bytes >>>

###
# battery health (whole-machine)
POST {{host}}/api/items/SN:{{machineSerial}}/external-docs/intake-scans
X-Intake-Token: {{intakeToken}}
X-Filename: battery.txt
Content-Type: text/plain

<<< raw battery report bytes >>>

###
# --- Per-component reports → aggregate on the DRIVE component (by serial) ----
#   While the drive is in-device these surface on the parent (aggregated);
#   after Zerlegung they surface on the drive's own standalone item — same
#   files, no move, because storage is serial-keyed.

# SMART for drive 0
POST {{host}}/api/items/SN:{{disk0Serial}}/external-docs/intake-scans
X-Intake-Token: {{intakeToken}}
X-Filename: smart-nvme0n1.txt
Content-Type: text/plain

<<< raw smartctl -a output for drive 0 >>>

###
# wipe certificate for drive 0 (travels with the drive on graduation)
POST {{host}}/api/items/SN:{{disk0Serial}}/external-docs/intake-scans
X-Intake-Token: {{intakeToken}}
X-Filename: wipe-certificate-nvme0n1.txt
Content-Type: text/plain

<<< raw wipe/erasure certificate for drive 0 >>>

###
# SMART for drive 1
POST {{host}}/api/items/SN:{{disk1Serial}}/external-docs/intake-scans
X-Intake-Token: {{intakeToken}}
X-Filename: smart-sda.txt
Content-Type: text/plain

<<< raw smartctl -a output for drive 1 >>>

###
# wipe certificate for drive 1
POST {{host}}/api/items/SN:{{disk1Serial}}/external-docs/intake-scans
X-Intake-Token: {{intakeToken}}
X-Filename: wipe-certificate-sda.txt
Content-Type: text/plain

<<< raw wipe/erasure certificate for drive 1 >>>


###############################################################################
# NOT part of the intake image (operator web app, listed for completeness)
#   • Zerlegung / graduation (set identity write-once + extract) and
#   • manual "add unidentified component" / component deletion
#   run from the web UI, not the netboot image. See component-lifecycle.md §4.
###############################################################################

# Auth note: all /api/intake/* routes require X-Intake-Token when INTAKE_TOKEN
# is set (all requests accepted when it is unset — dev mode). The external-docs
# endpoint keeps its own existing auth.
